  "scope": "R459 and R461 refine the accepted-coordinate indexed tape and stopping count in the abstract list/tape model. R460 relates the decoded eight-word block, initial acceptance result, and scan count to that model under a position-sensitive family of accepted-value permutations. R462 lifts that block permutation into the source-shaped index-8 refill relation: calls, result, carry state, transformed block, and stopping index are related; adaptive-prefix preservation still assumes explicit Freshness. R463 connects the number of accepted entries in the prefix of length optionCount to whether the first accepted entry is present, and gives the corresponding offset rule for dropping that prefix.",
  "first_remaining": "Prove the actual four-coordinate execution/tape law: the eight decoded block coordinates are distributed according to the modeled accepted-coordinate tape, with source cursor, shared-oracle queries, cached values, sentinel skips, and refill chronology preserved. No actual four-limb uniform law is established here."
